&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Abacus Insights is transforming how data and AI work for health plans. Our mission is simple: make healthcare data usable, so the people responsible for care and cost decisions can act faster, with confidence.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;As the AI and Data Platform for Payer Intelligence, we help health plans break down data silos to create a single, trusted data foundation. That foundation powers better decisions—so plans can improve outcomes, reduce waste, and deliver better experiences for members and providers alike. Backed by $100M from top investors, we&#39;re tackling big challenges in an industry that&#39;s ready for change. Our platform enables GenAI use cases by delivering clean, connected, and reliable healthcare data to support automation, prioritization, and decision workflows—and it&#39;s why we are leading the way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Our innovation begins with people. We are bold, curious, and collaborative—because the best ideas come from working together. We embrace the thoughtful use of AI and automation to drive innovation and efficiency, and we look for individuals who are curious and adaptable—those excited to leverage emerging technologies to enhance how we work—while keeping human insight, connection, and our clients at the center of every decision.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Ready to make an impact? Join us and let&#39;s build the future together.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an experienced Business and Data Analyst to join our team. In this role, you&#39;ll be the analytical engine between a client&#39;s business need and the data solution that delivers it. You&#39;ll turn business questions into precise, testable requirements, then use the data itself to prove out what&#39;s possible: profiling sources, validating assumptions, and shaping designs that are clean, buildable, and grounded in evidence rather than opinion. You&#39;ll own the requirements and analysis for your use cases and workstreams, working in close partnership with Business Solution Managers who hold the broader engagement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Doing that well takes two things at once: command of healthcare business context, and deep, hands-on fluency in the data. This is a client-facing role. You&#39;ll translate complex healthcare challenges into rigorous requirements, and you&#39;ll use SQL and analytical judgment to show clients and delivery teams what the data actually says, where it falls short, and what that means for the design.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;No engagement lives in isolation. A data model built for one client&#39;s use case can share structure with a completely different client&#39;s need; a transformation rule written for one state&#39;s requirements often anticipates the next state&#39;s. You&#39;ll learn to see each requirement as part of a larger system of clients, states, use cases, and data flows, and to flag where a design can be reused or where it could collide with other work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our clients are US health plans and the partners who serve them, and the engagements span everything it takes to make their data usable. That can mean standardizing and migrating data onto a new platform, meeting evolving regulatory and compliance mandates, or powering the broader analytics and reporting programs that drive payer performance across Medicare, Medicaid, and Commercial lines of business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your day to day&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analyze the Data and Build the Evidence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write and execute SQL daily to profile source data, test assumptions, quantify data quality (completeness, validity, uniqueness, consistency, timeliness), and prototype logic before it reaches the build team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze source data to establish what is actually available and reliable: field population and distributions, key integrity, duplicates, outliers, and gaps against what the business use case needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reconcile and validate outputs against source systems and client-provided benchmarks (claim counts, member months, paid amounts, enrollment spans, provider rosters), investigating variances to root cause and documenting findings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and document business metrics and KPIs precisely: numerator, denominator, inclusion and exclusion logic, time basis, and grain, so every consumer of the data calculates and reads them the same way.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform exploratory and root-cause analysis on client questions and data anomalies, and turn findings into clear, quantified recommendations for client and internal audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Summarize findings through data profiling reports, analysis readouts, and visualizations that make the story clear to non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Requirements and Design for Your Use Cases&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead discovery sessions for your use cases, and support broader engagement-level sessions alongside the Business Solution Manager, to understand the why and what behind each use case: the business context, pain points, expected outcomes, and success criteria, rather than just the surface-level data ask.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate each use case into clear, testable requirements, including success criteria and non-functional requirements, and maintain traceability from business need to requirement to design to test.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data analysis to sharpen and challenge requirements: confirm that what the client is asking for is supported by the data they have, and surface gaps early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document source-to-target mappings, transformation logic, and business rules that developers can build from, and define the test conditions and expected results QA will use to validate them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recommend the appropriate grain and structure of a dataset given the business context, and analyze how that grain decision ripples into the downstream reports, models, or programs that consume the data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify dependencies before a design is finalized: which other workstreams, reports, or client use cases touch this same data, and how a change here could break or benefit them, escalating cross-workstream impacts to the Business Solution Manager.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply systems thinking: recognize when a design built for one client, state, or use case can become a reusable pattern, and raise and shape that reuse rather than discovering it in hindsight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be a Trusted Client-Facing Partner&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive requirements-gathering and clarification conversations with client SMEs for your use cases, since incomplete or poorly elicited requirements undermine everything built downstream.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present analysis results, data quality findings, and recommendations to client stakeholders with clarity and confidence, and guide decisions with evidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent client intent for your use cases through delivery and serve as a day-to-day point of contact, with the Business Solution Manager owning the overall client relationship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate fluently between business and technical audiences, so both sides share the same understanding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate Across Delivery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect the client and the internal team on your workstreams, holding the business context, data findings, and design drivers that shape the build.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the business and data analysis SME for Solution Architects, Product, QA, Account Management, and Program Management, giving them clean hand-offs with the context, business rules, and analysis they need to execute without rework or reinterpretation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support QA and UAT by supplying validation queries, expected results, and variance analysis, and by helping triage defects to business rule, mapping, or source data causes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain awareness of the wider engagement: understand how a decision made for one workstream affects the others, and flag those ripple effects before they surface as rework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring to the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree, or equivalent relevant experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years working in the US healthcare domain and with healthcare data (claims, provider, membership/eligibility, benefits, prior authorization, or PBM).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Payer experience required: direct experience working with or for a US health plan (Medicare, Medicaid, or Commercial), whether in-house or through healthcare consulting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working command of core payer concepts such as membership/enrollment, provider, claims, and authorizations, enough to reason about business context rather than specialize narrowly in any one area.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong, hands-on SQL: comfortable with joins across large, multi-table datasets, window functions, CTEs, aggregations, and date/span logic, used regularly to profile, validate, reconcile, and analyze data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated analytical rigor: a track record of profiling data, assessing data quality, investigating anomalies to root cause, and communicating quantified findings that drove a decision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience defining metrics, mentoring junior analysts, and eliciting and authoring business requirements in complex, data-driven environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident client-facing communication; able to drive a conversation, elicit requirements clearly, and present analytical findings to technical and non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating with ambiguity and re-prioritizing frequently while managing multiple use cases within a larger engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing systems thinking: experience designing for reuse and scale across states, clients, or use cases rather than solving each case in isolation, and the ability to trace how a requirement or data model decision affects other parts of a larger data ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we would like to see, but not required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to Databricks or Snowflake&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with BI and visualization tools (e.g., Tableau, Power BI, or similar) to communicate analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with HEDIS and Stars quality reporting, risk adjustment, payment integrity, value-based care analytics, provider data management, or CMS interoperability (CMS-0057).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of data modeling concepts, including how the grain and structure of a dataset shape its downstream use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Python or similar for analysis and automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Compensation for this role is based on experience, skills, and location, and includes base salary plus eligibility for performance bonuses and equity grants.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll get in return&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive Leave &amp;amp; Benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive health coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equity for every employee&amp;nbsp;– share in our success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growth-focused environment – your development matters here&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work arrangements&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Standard hours: 9 hours/day, 5 days/week&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Location: Pune, Onsite (1 PM - 10 PM IST)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shift: Your standard working hours will be nine (9) hours per day within the Company’s standard working hours.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Specific working hours may vary based on business needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment as an Equal Opportunity Employer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;As a mission-led technology company helping to drive better healthcare outcomes, Abacus Insights believes that the best innovation and value we can bring to our customers comes from diverse ideas, thoughts, experiences, and perspectives. Therefore, we dedicate resources to building diverse teams and providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants. Abacus prohibits discrimination and harassment regarding race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local laws.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;At the heart of who we are is a commitment to continuously and intentionally building an inclusive culture—one that empowers every team member across the globe to do their best work and bring their authentic selves. We carry that same commitment into our hiring process, aiming to create an interview experience where you feel comfortable and confident showcasing your strengths. If there’s anything we can do to support that—big or small—please let us know.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;AI Use in Recruitment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;We use AI-powered tools throughout our recruitment process. This includes Greenhouse&#39;s Real Talent Matching Technology, which helps prioritize applications based on job-related criteria, as well as additional AI tools used to support sourcing, interview preparation, and other recruiting tasks. &lt;strong&gt;We do not remove the human element—our recruiters and hiring teams review all applications and make all decisions related to candidate progression and hiring, regardless of which tools are used to support that process.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;elementToProof&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Identity and Location Verification&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;elementToProof&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;elementToProof&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;To protect the integrity of our hiring process, all interviews are conducted by live video with your camera on. Virtual or blurred backgrounds and headsets are not permitted absent an approved accommodation, and you should be in a well-lit, private space where your face and surroundings are clearly visible. Candidates who advance may also be asked to complete identity and location verification, which may include verifying your identity, work history, and confirming that you are located where your application states. Applications containing knowingly false or materially misrepresented information, including identity, location, or credentials, may be disqualified, and any offer may be rescinded if a material misrepresentation is discovered at any point in the process.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;elementToProof&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;elementToProof&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;I&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;f you need an accommodation for any part of the interview process, please let your recruiter know in advance.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;elementToProof&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;elementToProof&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;By applying, you acknowledge that we will collect and process your personal information for recruiting purposes in accordance with applicable data protection laws, including for the verification steps described above. Please review our&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a id=&quot;OWA4b048287-23b9-797d-9e94-700349584c71&quot; class=&quot;OWAAutoLink&quot; href=&quot;https://nam12.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fabacusinsights.com%2Fapplicant-privacy-policy%2F&amp;amp;data=05%7C02%7Cheidi.weinstein%40abacusinsights.com%7C7d44e83a2b7f4081beae08df23b25d49%7C0819ed188d9747bb930bec1982f9aa76%7C0%7C0%7C639268921130656820%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C4000%7C%7C%7C&amp;amp;sdata=d%2BoHUdDyVi5syk0k8eO7f73azMYj8kBhPCDKTMK%2Fcvo%3D&amp;amp;reserved=0&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;e27af475-00b4-404d-99eb-63a7d6967b53&quot;&gt;Applicant Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;for more information, including your rights.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Abacus Insights is transforming how data and AI work for health plans. Our mission is simple: make healthcare data usable, so the people responsible for care and cost decisions can act faster, with confidence.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;As the AI and Data Platform for Payer Intelligence, we help health plans break down data silos to create a single, trusted data foundation. That foundation powers better decisions—so plans can improve outcomes, reduce waste, and deliver better experiences for members and providers alike. Backed by $100M from top investors, we&#39;re tackling big challenges in an industry that&#39;s ready for change. Our platform enables GenAI use cases by delivering clean, connected, and reliable healthcare data to support automation, prioritization, and decision workflows—and it&#39;s why we are leading the way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Our innovation begins with people. We are bold, curious, and collaborative—because the best ideas come from working together. We embrace the thoughtful use of AI and automation to drive innovation and efficiency, and we look for individuals who are curious and adaptable—those excited to leverage emerging technologies to enhance how we work—while keeping human insight, connection, and our clients at the center of every decision.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Ready to make an impact? Join us and let&#39;s build the future together.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Senior Business Intelligence Analyst (Healthcare) to join our Growth Analytics team. This role is ideal for a data professional with 4–5 years of experience who is passionate about turning healthcare data into decisions that drive revenue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be the analytics engine behind our go-to-market motion. You will build the AI-assisted dashboards, forecasts and models that tell leadership where the pipeline stands, where margin is made, and where the next opportunity is. You will also provide hands-on sales operations support to the Sales Director team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Success in this role looks like dashboards and analysis that leaders rely on, a trusted reputation as the go-to partner for sales and growth analytics, and the ability to turn complex healthcare data into clear, compelling narratives. You will thrive if you bring curiosity, learning agility and a proactive approach in a fast-paced, high-growth environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Day to Day&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Growth analytics and business intelligence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build and maintain AI-assisted dashboards, KPIs and executive reporting in BI tools (Power BI or Tableau), SQL and Excel to track pipeline, bookings, revenue and sales performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI and agentic tools to accelerate analysis, automate recurring reporting and data preparation, and generate insights and narrative summaries, applying human judgment to validate accuracy before anything reaches leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze pipeline, historical and real-time data to surface trends, develop forecasts, and inform pipeline and revenue planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build revenue, cost and deal-margin models, and support pricing analysis for our healthcare data products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare the data, analytics and demo materials that showcase our payment integrity, medical cost management, value-based care, population health, risk adjustment and HEDIS/Star offerings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide data and analysis for RFPs and proposals so that every number holds up to scrutiny&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track payer, market, competitor and regulatory trends, and translate findings into actionable insights for Sales, Product and executive leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure data accuracy and consistency across systems, reports and dashboards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales operations support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain CRM documentation and data hygiene, and troubleshoot CRM and tooling issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support weekly sales calls and pipeline reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist the Sales Director team with demo environments, sales collateral, and ad hoc deal and account analytics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create executive presentations and sales decks with clear, data-driven narratives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with Sales, Finance and GTM teams on analysis and strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring to the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4–5 years of relevant experience in analytics, business intelligence, consulting or sales operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2–3+ years working in US healthcare or healthcare data/analytics (payer, provider, vendor, health-tech or consulting)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong SQL skills and hands-on experience building dashboards in a BI tool such as Power BI or Tableau&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience using AI and agentic AI tools (such as Claude, ChatGPT or Copilot) to build, automate or accelerate analytics and reporting work, with sound judgment about validating AI-generated output&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Excel proficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Baseline financial and business acumen: comfortable with unit economics, margin, pricing and financial reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to synthesize data into insights and executive-ready communication, both written and verbal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated learning agility, problem-solving ability and attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Business, Economics, Analytics or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Would Like to See, but Not Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with payer claims data, healthcare financial concepts or payment integrity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience reporting from a CRM such as Salesforce or HubSpot&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or configuring AI agents, automated workflows or integrations (for example via MCP, APIs or low-code tools)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to cloud data platforms and modern data stack tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Get in Return&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive leave and benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive health coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equity for every employee – share in our success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growth-focused environment – your development matters here&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Arrangements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Standard hours: 9 hours/day, 5 days/week&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Location: Remote; must be able to work U.S. hours (Eastern Time)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shift: This role requires alignment with U.S. business hours (Eastern Time) to support the Growth Analytics and Sales leadership teams in real time. Specific working hours may vary based on business needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment as an Equal Opportunity Employer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;As a mission-led technology company helping to drive better healthcare outcomes, Abacus Insights believes that the best innovation and value we can bring to our customers comes from diverse ideas, thoughts, experiences, and perspectives. Therefore, we dedicate resources to building diverse teams and providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants. Abacus prohibits discrimination and harassment regarding race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local laws.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;At the heart of who we are is a commitment to continuously and intentionally building an inclusive culture—one that empowers every team member across the globe to do their best work and bring their authentic selves. We carry that same commitment into our hiring process, aiming to create an interview experience where you feel comfortable and confident showcasing your strengths. If there’s anything we can do to support that—big or small—please let us know.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;AI Use in Recruitment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;We use AI-powered tools throughout our recruitment process. This includes Greenhouse&#39;s Real Talent Matching Technology, which helps prioritize applications based on job-related criteria, as well as additional AI tools used to support sourcing, interview preparation, and other recruiting tasks. &lt;strong&gt;We do not remove the human element—our recruiters and hiring teams review all applications and make all decisions related to candidate progression and hiring, regardless of which tools are used to support that process.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;elementToProof&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Identity and Location Verification&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;elementToProof&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
